body:
@calmh the XDG anti-pattern is a technical debt. I suspect we will continue to see these kind of issues reported from ST users until the issue is fixed.

There are indeed log files stored in the default installation.

![image](https://github.com/syncthing/syncthing/assets/6200749/b3d024ee-a2ed-42e9-96bb-0c4dcfd62ead)

@calmh 

> If there's a log file there it's because you manually asked for it, we don't default to using any log file on unixes.

I didn't ask for this path specifically, the command run by `syncthing-start.desktop` is `syncthing […] --logfile=default`, so it **is** syncthing that selects this bogus path, not me.
